---
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
import Link from "../components/Link.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/custom.css";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Navbar />
  <div class="page" data-pagefind-body data-pagefind-meta="category:Marketing">
    <!-- Intro Section -->
    <header
      class="section-wrapper texture-607"
    >
      <section class="section intro-section">
        <h1 class="heading-1">Build reusable, automated workflows</h1>
        <p class="paragraph-xl">
          Stop reinventing the wheel on every project. Automate repetitive tasks
          and build workflows that evolve with your practice.
        </p>
      </section>
    </header>

    <!-- Problem & Data Flow -->
    <div
      class="section-wrapper texture-232-k"
    >
      <section class="section">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <Card>
            <h3 class="heading-3">
              The problem: too much <em>manual work</em>
            </h3>
            <p class="paragraph-sm">
              Geotechnical engineering projects involve repetitive tasks that
              could be automated:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-4 space-y-1 text-base">
              <li>Manually copying data between formats</li>
              <li>Recreating similar analyses for each project</li>
              <li>Re-exporting data when requirements change</li>
              <li>Rebuilding visualizations from scratch</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="paragraph-sm mt-4">
              The underlying issue: data trapped in proprietary formats and
              disconnected tools makes automation difficult.
            </p>
          </Card>

          <Card>
            <h3 class="heading-3">
              Engineering projects as <em>data flow graphs</em>
            </h3>
            <p class="paragraph-sm">
              Essential to bringing automation and computational design to
              geotechnical engineering is recognizing that engineering projects
              can be represented as data flow graphs:
            </p>
            <pre
              class="bg-gray-3 px-4 py-3 rounded mt-4 text-sm font-mono">data → process → data → process → data</pre>
            <p class="paragraph-sm mt-4">
              The whole project can be seen as one large process:
            </p>
            <pre
              class="bg-gray-3 px-4 py-3 rounded mt-4 text-sm font-mono">inputs → engineering process → deliverables</pre>
          </Card>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- Workflow Breakdown & Foundation -->
    <div class="section-wrapper texture-616">
      <section class="section">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <Card>
            <h3 class="heading-3">
              Break down workflows into <em>smaller steps</em>
            </h3>
            <p class="paragraph-sm">
              This large process can be broken down into smaller steps, each with
              clear inputs and outputs. This makes it possible to:
            </p>

            <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
              <div>
                <strong>1. Identify what's worth automating</strong>
                <p class="text-sm mt-1">
                  Not everything needs automation. Some parts are iterative,
                  require human judgment, or are genuinely messy. Breaking down
                  the workflow helps you identify the repetitive, rule-based parts
                  worth automating.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <strong>2. Automate incrementally</strong>
                <p class="text-sm mt-1">
                  Start with one manual process. Replace it with a script. Test it
                  on a project. Refine it. Move to the next process.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <strong>3. Build reusable components</strong>
                <p class="text-sm mt-1">
                  As scripts mature, split them into smaller, single-purpose
                  functions. Single-purpose functions are easier to maintain and
                  reusable across projects.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <strong>4. Chain processes together</strong>
                <p class="text-sm mt-1">
                  For parts of your workflow with clear, unidirectional data flow,
                  mature functions can be chained into Directed Acyclic Graphs
                  (DAGs) that automatically rerun when inputs change.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </Card>

          <Card>
            <h3 class="heading-3">
              The foundation: <em>structured, accessible data</em>
            </h3>
            <p class="paragraph-sm">
              Automating processes without structured input data is impossible.
              Ground investigation data needs to be:
            </p>

            <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-4 space-y-2 text-base">
              <li>
                <strong>Structured</strong> - Following the natural hierarchy (projects
                → boreholes → samples → tests)
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Accessible</strong> - In formats that work with modern tools
                and programming languages
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Validated</strong> - With relationships properly enforced
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p class="paragraph-sm mt-4">
              This is where geospatial databases and open standards become
              essential.
            </p>
          </Card>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- How We Help -->
    <div
      class="section-wrapper texture-607"
    >
      <section class="section">
        <Card variant="featured">
          <h3 class="heading-2">How we help</h3>
          <p class="paragraph">
            We provide consulting and software solutions for teams building
            automated workflows:
          </p>

          <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-6 space-y-2 text-base">
            <li>
              <strong>Data conversion and structuring</strong> - Transform industry-specific
              formats (AGS, GEF, gINT, Excel) into structured geospatial databases
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Workflow automation</strong> - Build custom scripts and tools
              for repetitive processes
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Integration</strong> - Connect geotechnical data with GIS tools,
              Python scientific ecosystem, and BIM platforms
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Training and guidance</strong> - Help your team adopt computational
              design practices
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p class="paragraph mt-6">
            Whether you're comfortable with Python or need us to handle the
            technical implementation, we can help you move from manual workflows
            to automated, reusable processes.
          </p>

          <p class="paragraph mt-4">
            We bring specialized expertise in geospatial visualization
            technologies, industry data formats (AGS, GEF, BRO/XML), and
            computational tools like Grasshopper, PyVista, and Speckle. <Link
              href="/technologies">Learn more about our technical capabilities</Link
            >.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-8">
            <p class="font-bold text-lg">
              Contact us at <Link variant="email" href="mailto:info@bedrock.engineer"
                >info@bedrock.engineer</Link
              > to discuss your workflow automation needs.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
              Or explore the open-source library that powers these solutions: <Link
                href="https://github.com/bedrock-engineer/bedrock-ge"
                >bedrock-ge on GitHub</Link
              >
            </p>
          </div>
        </Card>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- CTA Section -->
    <div
      class="section-wrapper texture-232-k"
    >
      <section class="section cta-section">
        <h2 class="heading-2">Ready to automate your workflows?</h2>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Let's discuss how we can help transform your geotechnical practice with
          automation and structured data.
        </p>
        <Link
          variant="email"
          href="mailto:info@bedrock.engineer"
          class="mt-4 text-xl">Get in touch</Link
        >
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
